🌐 MVP Features
1. Register an Instrument
User Flow:
User lands on "Register" page.
User provides:
Instrument name (e.g., "Proclamation of The New Kybalion").
Content (either:
Paste a CID (from Pinata/IPFS).
Upload a file (auto-generates CID via Pinata).
Paste raw text (auto-generates SHA-256 digest as a placeholder CID).
Tri-Vector coordinates (optional, defaults to `commons-vector-v1`):
`tri_vector` (Identity, e.g., `1a0de0b-f30c`).
`spatial_vector` (Location, e.g., `7e34-88a8`).
`rule_vector` (Interpretation, e.g., `057e4f535abc`).
Previous instrument (CID or digest of the prior instrument, or `"GENESIS"`).
User clicks "Register".
System:
Generates a CID (if file/text is provided).
Derives a Composite Key:
```
Composite Key = SHA512(CID + ":" + spatial_vector + ":" + rule_vector)
```
Signs the composite key with Ed25519 (user provides a private key or generates one in-browser).
Creates a CVP Instrument (`.car.json` format) and stores it in localStorage (or pins to IPFS if user opts in).
Displays the instrument details (CID, Composite Key, Signature, etc.).
